{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-A-glm53flash-max-std-full200-20261010","prediction_set_name":"glm53flash-max-std-full200-20261010","paper_id":"2604.26993","judge_input_sha256":"dbea4e3d02286b1f32936f7e4d3702c9c03193dfe6fce77be5f2ba02ee289dd1","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I001:U001","2604.26993:I001:U002","2604.26993:I001:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns applying a finite-horizon tracking estimate without establishing that perturbed trajectories remain in its continuity domain K. ISSUE-001 instead concerns an overbroad strict-inwardness claim at stationary boundary points; it does not diagnose the missing trajectory-domain hypothesis.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I002:U001","2604.26993:I002:U002","2604.26993:I002:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the unclosed nonstationary equality case 4||a_t||^2-delta=0 in the rank-1 approximation boundary-inward proof. ISSUE-001 identifies a different defect involving stationary boundary points and the remark's quantifier, not the approximation proposition's nonstationary equality case.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"shared_topic_or_location_only","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I003:U001","2604.26993:I003:U002","2604.26993:I003:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns overstating finite-horizon numerical trajectories as evidence of asymptotic unboundedness. ISSUE-001 concerns strict inward mapping at stationary boundary points and contains no diagnosis of the empirical or asymptotic inference.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I004:U001","2604.26993:I004:U003","2604.26993:I004:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is a scalar threshold endpoint where a nonstationary boundary point has zero certificate change, undermining stationarity-equality and uniqueness claims. ISSUE-001 instead diagnoses stationary points that are fixed by the gradient step in a broader remark.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"no_substantive_overlap","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I005:U001","2604.26993:I005:U002","2604.26993:I005:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the missing proof that every arbitrary nonterminal level contains the required unbalanced global minimizer. ISSUE-001 does not address level coverage, minimizer existence, or the resulting uniqueness argument.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I006","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"no_substantive_overlap","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I006:U001","2604.26993:I006:U002","2604.26993:I006:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is nonuniqueness under increasing reparameterization of the state coordinate, exhibited by P_h(delta). ISSUE-001 contains no diagnosis of parameter-coordinate freedom or the failure of numerical uniqueness.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.26993:I007","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.26993:I007:U001","2604.26993:I007:U002","2604.26993:I007:U003","2604.26993:I007:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U007"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"Both entries concern the strict-inwardness remark, but the gold defect is the approximation endpoint q_{eta'}(delta_t)=0, where a nonstationary boundary point can have equality. ISSUE-001 only identifies stationary boundary points as a counterexample to the unrestricted 'any point' wording and does not recognise the distinct q=0 endpoint failure.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}